			"id": "agent-analysis-uiability-lifecycle-windowstage-callbacks",
			"interpretation": "This Stage-model sample teaches the UIAbility lifecycle. Responsibility: keep the teaching unit coherent - EntryAbility.ets overrides onCreate, onWindowStageCreate/WillDestroy/Destroy, onForeground, onBackground, onDestroy and onNewWant, pairing windowStage.on('windowStageEvent') logging with off in onWindowStageWillDestroy via stored this.windowStage. Boundary: leaf project at Ability/UIAbilityLifecycle owning hvigor/oh-package configs, app/module json5, tests, resources and SDK contract (compatibleSdkVersion 6.0.2(22), modelVersion 5.0.5). Relations: module.json5 binds mainElement/srcEntry to EntryAbility and pages to $profile:main_pages, whose sole route pages/Index is what onWindowStageCreate loads; README_zh.md and the [Start/End] snippet markers mirror the callbacks one-for-one, so renaming callbacks or moving srcEntry/routes demands synchronized updates to module.json5, main_pages.json, README_zh.md and markers. Behavior claims are textual: on/off pairing, error-logged loadContent, an ohosTest starting EntryAbility by name and asserting it is the top ability. Contract: keep callback names, srcEntry, Index route, markers, README steps and on/off pairing consistent.",
			"kind": "analysis",
